menu "Sorting Camera"

    config SORTING_CAM_FRAME_TRANSPORT
        bool "Enable TCP/UDP frame transport"
        default n
        help
            Starts the raw frame transport (TCP listener on STREAM_TRANSPORT_PORT and
            a UDP receive socket) in addition to the HTTP baseline. The HTTP
            baseline (status/snapshot/config on port 80, MJPEG on port 81) is the
            only path used by the desktop app and the benchmark harness, and the
            transport permanently consumes two lwIP sockets (7 + 5 = 12 sockets for
            the two HTTP servers, 14 with the transport enabled). Leave this off
            unless a raw-transport client is being used; raise
            CONFIG_LWIP_MAX_SOCKETS if you enable it.

endmenu
